      "writtenOn": "2019-12-20T16:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m still concerned with the duplication between here and GenerateAndroidBuildActions.  It will be easy to make a change to the logic there without updating here, which will result in misleading deps info.\n\nMaybe instead of using WalkDeps to recurse to find the static libraries, modules that are apex variants could walk their own static dependencies in their own GenerateAndroidBuildActions and store the result on their Module, and then you can just query that instead of recursing into them?  That style often works better than WalkDeps, although it ends up distributing the code across more files.",
      "parentUuid": "20971ccb_f3bfb790",
